# WP Introspection (Generic Component Rules)

## Component surfaces to scan
- Runtime: registered blocks, styles, variations (if helper plugin installed)
- Files: block.json, patterns, templates, template parts, partials/components, CSS/JS
- Content DB: post_content block markup, known builder meta (best-effort)

## Intent-based theme routing
- If the user asks about active theme tokens, helpers, or design system details, use `get_theme_profile`.

## Variant mechanisms (generic)
- block styles (is-style-*)
- block variations
- pattern variants (multiple similar patterns)
- template part variants (header-compact, footer-legal)
- CSS modifiers (component--compact, is-variant-x)
- theme mods/options controlling rendering

## Design bridge (Figma / screenshot → repo conventions)
- Before creating new presentation code from a mock, run the design bridge workflow and reconcile tokens against `get_theme_profile` / bridge output.
- Never paste raw Figma hex, px spacing, or font stacks into theme files when preset CSS variables exist.

## Always output "why"
When suggesting reuse/extend/create, include:
- what exists
- where it lives
- how enabled
- why the recommended mechanism matches project conventions
